answers:
It's because your orders table has a field called customer that is the same to relationship name in Order model. So when you call $order->customer, it will get the value of this field. In your case, it is 20.
So, you can consider to change the customer field in orders table to customer_id or change the relationship method name in your model:
public function customerModel()
{
   return $this->belongsTo(Customer::class, 'customer');
}

So, then you can access the first name of the customer:
$order->customerModel->first_name

